{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat decisions/D028*; ls lab/jobs/job-34c09bec98 lab/jobs/job-a945fa8656; rg --files artifacts | rg '(loadmon|c1.*(order|text)|backend|34c09|a945)' | head -100; printenv LAB\"","aggregated_output":"# D028 — KV-cache precision as a memory lever (protocol frozen before results)\nQuestion: at long context, how much GPU memory does KV quantization save on Granite mixE4K, at what quality and speed cost? KV/token f16 = 24 layers x 2 x 8 kv-heads x 64 x 2 B = 48 KiB -> 1.5 GiB at 32k ctx (> mixE4K weights 779 MiB).\nImage: llamacpp-b0 (unpatched 31288c9c6). Tests lab/tests/kv1.json: decode/prefill at -c 32768 with the 1560-token prose prompt (-n 96) for KV f16/q8_0/q4_0 with -fa on, plus f16 -fa off control; 3 alternating rounds; PPL wikitext -c 4096 --chunks 6 per KV type.\nAccept a KV type as \"same accuracy\" if PPL within +1% of f16 (-fa on) AND greedy text identical or (if not) KLD check pending; report GPU delta MiB (nvidia-smi), prefill & decode t/s medians. Classification: representation (KV) trade-off — not an engine code gain.\nRESULT (job job-787f02f737, 7/15 clean; host monitor clean):\n- Quantized KV (q8_0, q4_0; -fa on) ABORTS at model load: ggml-impl.h:330 hash-set \"fatal error\" (SIGSEGV 139), in our b0 build AND the upstream ghcr full-cuda image at the same commit, with fit on or off, at 4k and 32k ctx -> engine defect in llama.cpp 31288c9c6 for this model/config, not our build. Delegated root cause: T-KVB. KV precision lever UNTESTED, not \"rejected\".\n- Flash attention alone (f16 KV, -c 32768, 1560-token prompt): GPU delta 2762 MiB (-fa on) vs 3746 MiB (-fa off) = -984 MiB; decode 627.2 vs 570.2 t/s (+10%), prefill 7001 vs 5865 t/s (+19%); text differs (96310158 vs f28de009; FA changes reduction order). PPL -c 4096 f16 FA 7.5385 (no non-FA PPL run -> quality equivalence of FA not measured here).\nClassification: memory-fit + speed observation for an exis